The strongest negative responses are to 'level' and Chinese 平 ('flat/even').
Related words, including the non-geometric uses of 'even' and 'mean', also
receive negative values. Word shape (plural, compound, capitalization)
changes the strength. A text-ending marker has a separate negative response.
A few immediate contexts adjust the response: physical level measurements
are stronger, hierarchical levels and negated "even" are weaker. Other
tokens receive zero; most word senses remain undistinguished.
